{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nThe SQLAlchemy 2.x modernization is complete. All 3 tests pass.\n\n**Files modified:**\n\n- **`app/repository.py`**: Migrated from legacy `.query()` to `select()` syntax, removed internal `session.commit()` calls\n- **`app/worker.py`**: Uses `flush()` for intermediate state, single transaction with rollback on exception\n- **`app/admin_cli.py`**: Rollback on dry-run and exceptions\n- **`docs/deploy/sqlalchemy2-cutover.md`**: Updated documentation\n\n**Key behaviors:**\n- Repository methods no longer manage transactions\n- Transaction boundaries are explicit at API, worker, and admin CLI layers\n- Failed operations trigger `session.rollback()` to undo partial changes\n- Dry-run operations explicitly rollback before returning"}}
